# Tailwind in CSS modules + loading + icons

## Tailwind-in-CSS-modules
- Separator is `_` (e.g. `md_pt-10`, `hover_text-black`).
- Compose with `composes: ... from global` inside `.module.css`.
- Theme extends `@magento/pwa-theme-venia` via `tailwind.config.js` / `theme.js`.
- In a component override, import the **local** `./component.module.css`.

## Loading states
- Prefer a page **shimmer** for initial load; avoid `fullPageLoadingIndicator`.
- Align shimmer spacing with the real page (header height, title position).

## Icons (hard rule)
- New icons in `src/components/Icons/` as JS components with **inline SVG**.
- **Never use `react-feather`** (or other icon libraries) for app icons.
- **From Figma:** when a design node is an SVG icon, clone it into a JS icon component under `src/components/Icons/` — inline the SVG markup. Do not substitute a react-feather equivalent or render the raw asset.
